// Jmoney — build configuration
//
// Supabase credentials live here, NOT in source code (master prompt §15). These
// values are substituted into Info.plist at build time as
//   JMoneySupabaseURL / JMoneySupabaseAnonKey
// and read at runtime by `SupabaseConfig`.
//
// This file is committed as an empty TEMPLATE. Fill it in locally and do not
// commit real values:
//
//   JMONEY_SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/your-project.supabase.co
//   JMONEY_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = eyJhbGciOi...
//
// NOTE: `//` starts a comment in an .xcconfig file, so a URL must be written
// with the empty `$()` between the slashes — `https:/$()/host` — to survive
// parsing. Writing `https://host` silently truncates the value at the slashes.
//
// The anon key is public by design (it ships in every Supabase client), but it
// is still configuration rather than code. The service-role key must NEVER be
// put here — the app has no use for it and it bypasses RLS.
//
// Leaving both values empty is supported: the app builds and runs with cloud
// sync disabled and says so in Settings, instead of failing to launch.

JMONEY_SUPABASE_URL =
JMONEY_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY =
